WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:21.029 align:start position:0%
 
born in germany she's a queen in ghana  10 years ago the villagers of rpu made  me their nana which means queen mother  in english it's sort of like the mother  of the tribe  it's one of the highest ranks in  traditional ghanaian society a political  office comparable to that of a cabinet  minister  bettina landcraft first came to ghana  over a decade ago  to the small village of apu a six-hour  drive from the country's capital akra  a trained nurse she came to work on a  christian aid project here  there's a steep drop behind you when you  drive around a particular bend in the  road the landscape opens up and you see  the lake  that was the first thing i saw  and when you stand on the mountain and  look down you also see the village  that was my first impression of our  people  the villagers live from farming and  fishing  bettina landcraft arrived in 2001 to  nurse the sick  at the time she had no idea that that  decision would change her life  and in this room we delivered the babies  we had some paracetamol a few band-aids  and some swabs but otherwise we just  muddled through  it was precisely this challenge and the  fascination of ghana that won  the villagers were so happy that i  decided to stay  and not just stay for a few days to get  an impression and then leave again  i think that was the most important  thing for them  it meant we were able to develop a  relationship from the start life  the role of queen was an honor bestowed  on her in part because of the practical  help she provides the villagers  in 2007 she founded the aid organization  madame fo ghana  madam fo is the ghanian word for friend  we need a lot of money a lot of money  so money  without funding bettina landcraft's  plans would remain dreams  emanuel stefansson and his team of aid  workers coordinate the projects for  which patina raises the cash  they first met in a pew  when i met her first time  i thought she is intelligent and  she she is very brave too  so we decided to work together  their first joint project was  constructing a well in a pew but that  was just the start  two years later bettina landgrafer was  named nana mother of the tribe  that changed her standing in the society  vip when we started the project we are  betina we are emmanuel but  as time comes on and they installed her  as a developing queen mother we started  calling her nana  yes  one of the reasons for bettina  landcraft's prestigious rank is her  ability to find sponsors in germany  their donations now provide basic  services in many areas of the ashanti  region  this village for instance now has public  the toilets are especially designed for  villages like this places that are off  the beaten track  it's not possible for a tanker to come  here and pump out the human waste at  regular intervals this way it can stay  here  these sanitary units are manufactured in  germany especially for regions like this  the composted waste can be used as  fertilizers  you can imagine the hygienic conditions  here there are about 250 villages if all  of them go into the bush every morning  and then it rains it gets spread all  over the village and that leads to  disease  the motor of this development program is  the german ghanaian aid organizat  the german partner provides the cash the  two directors in ghana organize the  projects  without german organization however it  might not work so well  i'm very impatient and i want to get  things done quickly  of course that doesn't always work here  but it's actually a very good character  trait because it enables you to get  things done  whereas other people might take their  time  but the fact is when somebody entrusts  us with money i have to see that it's  put to use soon and that the person who  donated the money sees a result as  quickly as possible  is on our way to see the district chief  in basome frejo  madame fogana coordinates its projects  with government programs  observing local courtesies is important  starting with the traditional greeting  okay  so what are they currently doing today  they're discussing the next stage in the  construction of the kindergarten in  danso village  the district chief appreciates the help  provided by madame fogana  but of course  at first when i heard of my madam for  ghana i thought he was a man  telling me honorable look who told me he  was a woman when i met her  i i just opened my mouth and said hey  then what man can do men to women who  can also do it  that's the reason why has been stood a  queen even he's working faster than even  the government himself  it's not unusual for aid organizations  to be quicker than governments in  getting things done  but having a government representative  publicly admitted is pretty rare that's  impressive  dunso is a small village in the ashanti  region  with support from adam fogana the  villagers are building this kindergarten  here  we negotiate with the villagers first  because it's their project  they submit a proposal to madame for  ghana  when we agree on what should happen we  call a meeting of the tribe and finally  decide when we will start the project  and who will be in charge  and when it's completed  the government supplies the teachers  or in the case of a hospital the nursing  staff  what is going on over here  the builders were trained by madame  fogana  that's good  it looks nice  which colors are we using yellow and red  we always paint the buildings brightly  and it's also important to show the  sponsors  we like to include the people who have  donated money in the painting  and below that comes madame for ghana so  it's clear which ngo built it  money money  in a pew and two neighboring villages  madame fogana provides school children  with a daily meal and medical services  this little boy for instance when you  look at his scalp you can see that he  has a skin infection it's the result of  unhygienic living conditions  means a lot to me partly because it was  introduced by the ghanaian government  their original intention was to persuade  more children to go to school by  offering them a school meal  but  generally don't eat breakfast  the children come to school hungry  the children often have to leave home  very early because they have a long walk  to school some more than an hour some  two hours they won't have had much  breakfast before leaving home at four in  the morning so when they arrive they're  really hungry and can't concentrate  during the day  all they can think about is their  evening meal so the school meals program  eases that situation  bettina landgraf had no intention of  finding love in ghana but it happened  anyway  ebenezer  is studying marketing me and bettina got  to know each other through madame for  ghana  um  have traveled from germany for the  queen's 10th anniversary celebrations  and to meet their daughter's fiancee  when you visit people in ghana you can't  just appear out of the blue and say hi i  came to see you  we first have to ask if we may enter the  property because it doesn't belong to us  even as a nana i simply can't go  wherever i want to  has  they begin with a traditional handshake  you take the plastic chairs  okay you can now sit down now that we're  all shaking hands  bettina will settle down a bit now that  she's engaged  she had various relationships in germany  but i had the feeling that this kind of  division in her life  having someone in germany and living her  life in ghana  it just couldn't work  for lunch there's fufu  cooked bananas and yam roots served with  a spicy sauce  but i really cherish how much we talk  it's maybe something you wouldn't expect  because we come from two completely  different universes as we say  i think it's great  in the ashanti culture people eat with  their fingers  has gotten used to it  and now she loves eating together out of  the same bowl  the questions will fall  for you to answer  as  a typical ashanti here i  advise her on so many things especially  about our cultures and also how to  relate to most of our people and also  how she has to go about the work that  she is doing here  this week bettina landcraft is  celebrating not only her 10th  anniversary as nana but also her  birthday  a party is being prepared down at the  lake  and the whole village is expected to  turn up  today bettina landcraft is torn between  two roles  that of a dignified queen and that of an  excited birthday girl  to you  today  her best friend alvira dusenberg has  come from germany to surprise her  she gets right into the spirit of things  have been close friends for 16 years  ever since they trained together as  pediatric nurses  but patina has changed a lot since she's  lived in ghana  elvira is somewhat perplexed by  bettina's role as nana  bettina's  in her heart bettina is bettina but she  has an entirely different position here  a completely different status  because she's a person who commands  respect here she adopts a very different  tone  and i don't feel so comfortable with  that  because i'm not familiar with that side  of her or the tone she uses to speak to  the workers to ensure that things get  done  it's late afternoon  some workers from the aid project are  trying to clear an area for the big  anniversary celebration  50 helpers from the local tribe who had  promised to give a hand have failed to  appear  i'm really cross because it's typical  people are simply not punctual they pay  no attention to the time  when they say we'll do it they mean  tomorrow morning  and it makes me furious because they  always rely on madame for ghana  the tribal chief is in for a reprimand  i'll give him a piece of my mind he  won't know what's hit him i just want to  strip off the chairman  is due to be inducted as paramount queen  tomorrow  that's a step higher in the hierarchy  but so far virtually no preparations  have been made  the sun is setting and still nothing has  been done  nobody knows where the sound system is  and there are no chairs with the guests  or decorations for the table of honor  but the villagers have a reputation of  doing everything at the last minute and  managing somehow  now it's morning in the palace of a pew  for everybody to know each other i want  everybody to mention his name and then  where he's coming from chief great chief  for this community i'll come once in a  while and look at them and i want us  to take these trees  representatives from the neighboring  villages receive mango trees as a symbol  of growth and prosperity  they're also a souvenir of the  celebrations  as mother of the tribe bettina landcraft  will have even more responsibility in  the future  when you've had an education and can  read and write when you've read books  and know something of the world you can  really give good advice here  even to people who are older and have a  lot more experience of life  the nurse from germany has earned great  respect here with her advice and counsel  i look different and was born somewhere  else and i have a different cultural  background  although i wouldn't say that now because  i've been here for 12 years i now  understand ghanaians better than germans  this attitude explains one of the  pediatric nurses favorite projects  the labor ward in dunkura  it's a separate wing of the public  hospital  fact is a  reason  the fact is there's tremendous need  patients who live far away in the bush  can't walk home  and if there are complications there is  simply no ward for them  they just give birth  and then have to go straight home  and in principle  gunny and women are traditionally cared  for by their relatives while they wait  to give birth  they often used to come to the clinic  too late  or leave it until the last minute  in this project come from ghana they  were trained here and most importantly  trained for their conditions here  there are lots of things in ghana that  you don't have in germany and vice versa  since the nana herself is a trained  nurse  the midwives really respect her  it  delivered just five  the families and the husbands don't  realize that there's a gigantic wound in  the belly they think the baby's out and  everything's fine they don't realize  that postnatal nursing is necessary  we can now prevent all the infections  that can occur after giving birth  because of unhygienic conditions  is also about boosting the women's  self-confidence  the clinic also provides education and  family planning so that the women and  their husbands can decide for themselves  how many children they want they now  have many choices which they didn't have  before  originally came to ghana to work for a  few weeks on a christian aid project  she's still a member of the lutheran  church but now feels drawn to buddhism  which shares many values with  christianity  i personally believe that jesus lived i  believe in jesus as a human being but i  also think he was a good buddhist  when i read the bible  i think that he realized buddhist values  completely  and villagers like this mixture  their christianity is blended with their  own traditional beliefs  and we pray when everything is completed  i wouldn't say that i identify with that  because as a buddhist i don't pray in  that way  but i think it's nice because it fosters  a sense of community  it's the morning of the great day in the  nana's palace  a good decade after being named queen  bettina landcraft will be proclaimed  paramount chief  that will give her the same status as  the other paramount chiefs of the region  some 35 villages are hoping that their  situation will improve through patina  lancafe's leadership and with sponsoring  from germany  after laya dama yamana  is a chief from the north  nana has been a role model  she has come to develop  ghana  and  in particular in my hometown  where i am the chief  she has put up a very nice clinic day  and  very soon i knew it will be turned to  fully fledged hospital  the procession heads towards the  ceremonial ground  amazingly everything's ready  overnight tents were erected and the  sound system installed  there's even a throne and chairs  some of the guests have traveled for  days to take part in this ceremony  and of course it begins with a  traditional handshaking  it's been a long week  the birthday the engagement the 10th  anniversary as nana and now the  induction as paramount queen this nurse  from germany has found a fulfilling life  in ghana  libations are poured to the tribal gods  and ancestors  and then they pray to the christian god  amen  reads her acceptance speech from an ipad  the paramount queen  does live in two worlds  has achieved many things for the people  here in the heart of ghana  but their expectations remain high  as paramount queen she won't be able to  fulfill all of them  but with the help of her adopted people  and the support of their german sponsors  she's determined to press ahead with her  development projects  you

